WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.975
- [Kelly] So Elizabeth
dropped out of school.

00:00:01.975 --> 00:00:02.808
- Yes she did.
- And I wanted

00:00:02.808 --> 00:00:04.290
to ask about this photo that you posted

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.910
'cause this feels like
you're back in school.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.110
Is this your school?
- I went back!

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.700
I went back to Allentown.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.100
I made it a point, I
kept having these dreams,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.990
you know, since I graduated which was,

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.110
I don't know, many years ago.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.129
- Yeah, just like a couple, yeah. (laughs)

00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:20.775
- Was it?

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:21.840
And, I was like, you know what?

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.910
I think I'm just gonna go
back and see the school

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:24.750
and see if they'll let me go

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.600
and it took me a while to
get somebody to call me back.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.140
I was like, I think this is
going to change something in me.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.640
I think the anxiety that I get,

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.655
the anxiety dreams that I get,

00:00:33.655 --> 00:00:36.360
I will no longer have if
I go and see it in person

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.130
and see what's changed and
support it and whatever,

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.840
and I did and they were awesome.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.990
I went to... My husband's a theater guy,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.820
and I was never in the
theater department in school.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.950
I did not act in school
'cause I was intimidated.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:47.820
- That's ironic!

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.069
- I know, it's weird.
- Okay.

00:00:49.069 --> 00:00:50.460
- It was weird, I was
only singing, though.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.860
I went and I saw this guy, Mr. Sackler,

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.640
whose like this local
famous theater director.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.630
And he was talking to me,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.950
he was like showing us the black box

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.000
and showing us all these cool things.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.290
It was like, this is the
show we're doing next

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.390
and my husband's like, wow,
what a cool school you went to!

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.094
And I was like, I was never
a part of any of this.

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:06.251
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:07.800
And he had no idea, and he mentioned me

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.640
and I had my mask on.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.473
- Wait, the teacher?

00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:10.560
- The teacher mentioned me.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.414
He's like, and Amanda Sey-

00:01:12.414 --> 00:01:13.920
And I pulled my mask down

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.080
and I was like, I should probably,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.660
I feel like I'm lying to you.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.830
And I took my mask down

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.990
and he screamed and ran across the room.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.480
And it was like the most
amazing thing I'd ever seen,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.250
most amazing like, reaction.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.480
And I realized-

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.313
- Aw, I love that he didn't know.

00:01:28.313 --> 00:01:30.360
- Yeah, and it was amazing for him.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.290
And I was like I'll come back

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.300
and talk to your theater
students 'cause like--

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.830
- Even if you have a
mask on, you have like,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.320
the most recognizable
eyes in all of the lands.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.241
Like, what?
(audience laughs)

00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:39.330
- I think he's just
super busy in his head.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.885
- Okay, I was like--
- I mean, he's amazing.

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.006
- [Kelly] He is not observant.

00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:43.238
- No!
- I was like, wait.

00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:45.870
- And I think he knows
that and it was so cute.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:47.284
He was like, ahhh!

00:01:47.284 --> 00:01:48.117
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:49.387
- I was like, oh my God, thank you.

00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:50.220
- [Kelly] Aw, I love that.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.429
- And so he lives with us now.

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:52.262
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:52.262 --> 00:01:53.902
Because it was very flattering.

00:01:53.902 --> 00:01:55.342
- He lives with us now.

00:01:55.342 --> 00:01:56.413
- No, but it was cool.

00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:58.410
Go back to high school if you can.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.310
If you were traumatized in
high school, try to go back.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.143
It might help.

00:02:03.143 --> 00:02:04.320
- I wasn't, what was traumatizing?

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.594
I wasn't traumatized, I
just didn't wanna be there.

00:02:06.594 --> 00:02:07.427
(audience laughs)

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.327
- I didn't wanna be there.
- That was it!

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.080
- It was girl stuff.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.550
- Oh, girls are mean.
- It was girl stuff.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.530
- See that's why, I had a few like,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.390
good, solid, like girlfriends.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.890
- I did too, I'm still best
friends with my girlfriend.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.090
We have a company together.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.320
We literally talk every day.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.460
- No people are mean, girls are mean.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.810
I will say that, girls are really mean.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:22.643
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:24.000
- And now if I run into them in town,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.680
we'll be like, oh hey, how are you doing?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.600
But like in high school it was like--

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.530
- I know, but here's the best part.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.850
Girl, you don't even
need to run into them.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.170
They can just watch you.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.823
Hey!
(audience applauding)

